A set name (dep) equal to an import qualifier that appears in BOTH the file being
overwritten (a_gen.go, which sorts lexically first) AND a hand-written sibling
(server.go). plumb records the sibling’s base rather than the output file’s (plumb
can rewrite imports in the output file, but not in the sibling), so the collision
is reported instead of silently emitted (Go forbids one identifier being both a
file-block import name and the package-block func).
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
output: a_gen.go
error-is: ErrSetNameCollision
-- example.com/dep/dep.go --
package dep

var Marker = 0
-- example.com/app/a_gen.go --
package app

import "example.com/dep"

var _ = dep.Marker
-- example.com/app/server.go --
package app

import "example.com/dep"

var Client = dep.Marker
-- example.com/app/providers.go --
package app

type Thing struct{}

//plumb:dep
func MakeThing() *Thing { return &Thing{} }
